  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable Cities: Tamale Urban Resilience Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Overall Objective &lt;/strong&gt;of the project is to improve urban sustainability and prosperity for all.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;specific objective&lt;/strong&gt; is to strengthen urban resilience to adapt to risks of climate change in Tamale particularly&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Following a city-wide analysis, the four proposed target districts - Lamakara, Bilpela, Tutingli and Nalung are located respectively in the south-western and southern parts of Tamale&apos;s urban area. These neighbourhoods illustrate the urban development issues facing the Tamale conurbation: they are poorly served by basic infrastructure and services (water shortage, lack of public spaces and difficult access to facilities). They are relatively dense and populated by a very young population. Economic opportunities are mainly concentrated in the informal private sector, which employs 80% of Tamale&apos;s working population, a proportion that is even higher among women.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Action will be implemented through 4 components:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Component 1. Investments to strengthen community resilience (20 MEUR)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This component is dedicated to financing works contracts, the technical engineering required for their completion, and the implementation of specific activities related to operation and maintenance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Component 2: Citizen participation and co-construction of solutions through an &#xbf;urban incubator&#xbf; approach (1,3 MEUR)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;An Urban Fabric Initiative (UFI) will be proposed to enhance the collaboration between the public authorities and the Civil Society Organisations (CSOs) in the project area. The UFI is an innovative scheme which intends to create and test urban micro-projects that are co-designed and implemented by the communities.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Component 3: Capacity-building for authorities (2,1 MEUR) &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A technical advisory and assistance firm for the Ministry and TaMA will be set up. The MLGCRA will be responsible for the contracting of this component and will work closely for the content with TaMA and AFD.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Component 4: Project management (3 MEUR&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#_msocom_1&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;[&lt;/a&gt;&lt;strong&gt;)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
